From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:13:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 376/376] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: describe the
 keyboard expander IRQ

The Wi-Fi service board deletes the AW9523 interrupt properties. That
keeps an unproven EINT out of the console path. No real-pad EINT has yet
been shown to fire on mainline MT6797: the lid's EINT5 never did, while
the PMIC's virtual EINT176 works.

Restore the INT description on the station: GPIO87 as EINT10, level
low, with the expander as an interrupt controller. pinctrl-aw9523 then
requests EINT10 at probe. It masks every pin interrupt until a consumer
requests one, so the line should stay idle while the matrix polls. The
keyboard keeps polling by default. Row interrupt mode is selected only
by rebinding the keyboard with the experiment-only override.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index e4578be77..1e3d607c6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -195,6 +195,19 @@ soc-critical {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Describe the AW9523 INT output again (GPIO87, EINT10, level low), which the
+ * Wi-Fi service board removes. The matrix still polls by default, and the
+ * expander masks every pin interrupt until a consumer requests one, so the
+ * line stays idle unless the keyboard is rebound in row interrupt mode.
+ */
+&aw9523 {
+	interrupt-parent = <&pio>;
+	interrupts = <10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+	interrupt-controller;
+	#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+};
+
 &thermal {
 	mediatek,toprgu = <&watchdog>;
 	mediatek,hw-reset-millicelsius = <117000>;
